   "source": [
    "## **I. Introduction**\n",
    "### **Background Information**\n",
    "In today's era of digital content explosion, YouTube stands as the world's largest video-sharing platform. Its \"Trending Videos\" list reflects the current focal points of public attention and cultural shifts. Understanding the characteristics of videos that successfully reach the trending list provides invaluable insights for content creators, digital marketers, and data enthusiasts alike.\n",
    "\n",
    "This project utilizes the YouTube Data API v3 to fetch real-time trending data from the United States (US) region, capturing key performance metrics such as view counts, like counts, comment counts, and publication timestamps.\n",
    "### **Project Goals**\n",
    "This project follows a structured data science workflow to address the following core questions:\n",
    "* **Data Correlation Analysis:** To determine whether there is a significant positive correlation between view counts and audience engagement metrics (e.g., Like Count).\n",
    "* **Upload Timing Insights:** To investigate whether there are specific distribution patterns in the upload times of trending videos (e.g., whether uploading during certain hours increases the likelihood of trending).\n",
    "* **Content Theme Synthesis:** To perform semantic analysis on trending video titles using a Large Language Model (LLM - Gemma3:4b), summarizing the core themes that currently drive high traffic.\n",
    "### **Methodology & Tech Stack**\n",
    "* **Data Extraction**: Integrated with the official YouTube API to retrieve live datasets.\n",
    "* **Data Cleaning**: Leveraged Pandas to filter out anomalies (such as videos with zero engagement metrics) and perform data type transformations.\n",
    "* **Analysis & Visualization**: Employed Matplotlib and Seaborn to generate scatter plots and histograms for quantitative data characterization.\n",
    "* **AI Integration**: Connected to a local Ollama service to implement automated data interpretation and generate comprehensive summary reports.\n",
    "### **How can you run this baby project:**\n",
    "1. **Download \"YTtop50_intheUS.csv\":**\n",
    "    * It is in the same file as this python project.\n",
    "    * Make sure the CSV is in the same file as the python file you're using while running the code.\n",
    "    * Do not rename the downloaded CSV file.\n",
    "2. **Download the packages you need**\n",
    "    * All you need are: pandas, matplotlib, seaborn, google-api-python-client, ollama. \n",
    "    * Run \"pip install pandas matplotlib seaborn google-api-python-client ollama\" if you don't have them.\n",
    "    * Run \"ollama pull gemma3:4b\" if you never try ollama gemma3 4b.\n",
    "4. **RUN CODE!**\n",
    "    * As you might not have YouTube API key to run the code using YouTube API, CSV version is provided. Please use the CSV one (cell number: II.3.b.)."
   ]
